  "limitations": [
    "The CSRF token and webhook admission windows are intentionally process-local for the single-process v1 API. They reset on process restart and do not provide a cross-process or distributed quota; a multi-process deployment must replace them with shared state and an appropriate session design.",
    "The API runs in direct mode and therefore rejects every Forwarded and X-Forwarded-* field. DEL-05 still owns the default runnable composition, listener and worker topology, and any future explicitly trusted reverse-proxy boundary; API-09 does not parse or trust proxy assertions.",
    "DEL-07 still owns the committed OpenAPI snapshot, generated TypeScript client, and drift gate. API-09 verifies and normalizes only the live FastAPI OpenAPI document and runtime response contract.",
    "The readiness probe's diagnostic 503 retains its established readiness payload rather than being rewritten as an application problem. Other installed API and framework failures pass through the shared application/problem+json occurrence boundary.",
    "The HTTP request timeout cancels downstream ASGI work and performs no automatic retry. If a downstream response has already started, the boundary propagates the timeout instead of attempting a second response; transport-level disconnect handling remains the server's responsibility.",
    "Runtime retry evidence applies only to persisted orchestrator-controlled READ and WRITE attempts. API-09 does not add route retries, provider SDK retries, background worker composition, or an implicit retry around non-idempotent effects.",
    "The webhook quota is keyed by authenticated source, and the v1 static registry enforces exactly one configured trigger per source. Invalid signatures consume no quota; rate denial occurs after authentication but before parsing or resolution and before any Work, Run, or receipt persistence or downstream work.",
    "DEL-04 owns migration and upgrade DDL for the new ingress.rate_limited audit-event database constraint. API-09 proves the constraint and repository behavior only against a fresh metadata-created SQLite schema; it does not claim an upgrade path for an existing database.",
    "Tests use local ASGI transports, SQLite-backed integration stores, deterministic adapters, and the repository network-denial fixture. No reverse proxy, multi-process server, PostgreSQL race, live provider, external webhook sender, or network fallback is exercised or claimed."
  ]
